<%# The browser's own inputs and outputs, moved here from the Walkboy panel.
    These are the devices a recording, a call or a stream captures and plays
    through: the same enumerateDevices() list, and the same one-device-per-kind
    choice jp.js reads with jawnosDevicePickGet() when it builds a getUserMedia
    constraint. It is deliberately separate from the machine's mixer above:
    the mixer's ids are the server's controllable devices, while these are the
    browser's own faces for the same room, so the label here may differ from
    the server's default. A press turns one device on and the rest of its kind
    off; the status attribute is what the picker draws. soundMediaRender is in
    sound.js, beside the label reader that already enumerated the same list. %>
    The rows draw the icon for the kind (microphone, camera or speaker) and the
    device's label; a label is blank until the browser has been granted media
    permission, so the row falls back to its kind and position. The status
    attribute is on for the picked device of each kind and off for the rest,
    and the global .media_picker handler writes the pick through stored.js.

<section class="sound_section sound_media_section" id="sound_media_section">
	<h3><%= &subs::ui('Media devices') %></h3>
	<div class="sound_browser"><%= &subs::ui('The inputs and outputs this browser uses for recordings and calls') %></div>
	<div class="sound_devices" id="sound_media_list"><p class="sound_empty"><%= &subs::ui('Reading the browser devices...') %></p></div>
	<div class="sound_browser"><%= &subs::ui('One device of each kind is on; the recordings and calls that start from this browser use those picks.') %></div>
</section>
<script>
	if (typeof soundMediaRender === 'function') { soundMediaRender(); }
</script>
